This one has been a long time in coming. The reason I held back with 
the summary is because I haven't quite fixed the problem but it is 
improved some.

Most of the assistance came from Dr Tom Blinn. He pointed out that i 
should check the gettydefs file for the definition on modem line. The 
definition now looks like this:
M57600# B57600 HUPCL CS8 CRTSCTS # B57600 SANE IXANY TAB3 HUPCL 
#login: #M38400

The CRTSCTS enables hardware flow control which is enabled on the 
modem. It wasn't there by default. 

As I said it hasn't completely removed the error but it is not as 
frequent as before.

Dp.



